\ scroll_hazel.6502 - step 2 layer 4: the scroll column's code that lives in HAZEL (decisions 38,
\ 39), after the compiled kinds (hazel_b, carried in MGAME after &4000 and copied in by
\ unpack_for_play with them). HAZEL is paged in through play (ACCCON's Y bit), whatever ROMSEL
\ holds, so this runs from the scroll with any bank paged; main RAM has no room for it.

\ pre_cancel: decision 38. A column built ahead in the wait (src/prebuild.6502) left the walk's
\ state in place for the scroll it was built for; for any other scroll (start_column), or when a
\ game starts or ends (reset_screen_scroll), the state goes back as it was. pre_valid 1 or &FF:
\ built, its state in place; 0 nothing built, &80 tried and already undone. ROMSEL and its MOS copy
\ are left as they came. A, X changed; Y kept.
.pre_cancel
{
    LDA pre_valid
    BEQ done
    CMP #&80
    BEQ done
    LDA os_ram_copy_of_currently_selected_rom
    PHA
    LDA #&04                        \ pre_undo is bank 4's, below &9000 (no ANDY)
    STA os_ram_copy_of_currently_selected_rom
    STA romsel
    JSR pre_undo
    PLA
    STA os_ram_copy_of_currently_selected_rom
    STA romsel
.done
    RTS
}

\ edge_right: calculate_screen_addresses_for_movers_on_edge's right edge (layer 4, decision 38's
\ commit). A mover is on the right edge only if its x is the edge's, so its x low byte is tested
\ first, unrolled: a mover that fails it is passed over, as the routine's own test would (its
\ only effects, &D0 and mover_width, are written again by the last mover's call, which is taken
\ in full as before). Movers that pass go through calculate_screen_addresses_for_mover_on_edge in
\ the same order as before (Y kept by it). Leaves Y = &21 and what that last call leaves.
.edge_right
{
    LDA edge_x_low
    FOR n = 0..&20
        CMP movers_x_low + n
        BNE * + 7
        LDY #n
        JSR hit
    NEXT
    LDY #&21
    JMP calculate_screen_addresses_for_mover_on_edge
.hit
    JSR calculate_screen_addresses_for_mover_on_edge
    LDA edge_x_low
    RTS
}

\ ground_square: multiply_A_by_X_2f1e for the ground's A = X = 0-3, leaving everything it leaves:
\ result_low X * X, result_high, multiplicand and multiplier_low 0, multiplier_high X; A = Y = 0;
\ Z set, N and C clear; V clear if X > 0 (its last ADC), else as it came; X kept.
.ground_square
{
    STX multiplier_high
    LDA squares,X
    STA result_low
    CPX #1
    BCC zero
    CLV
.zero
    LDA #0
    STA result_high
    STA multiplicand
    STA multiplier_low
    TAY
    CLC
    RTS
.squares
    EQUB 0, 1, 4, 9
}
